# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored) and edit as needed.
#
# Two independent knobs control where the sync runs and where the frontend
# tries to connect. They are NOT linked — set both consistently.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (Vite) → consumed by src/jazz/provider.tsx at build / dev-server time
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WebSocket URL the browser uses to reach the sync server.
#   - Default (no override): ws://localhost:4200
#   - For a phone / laptop on the same LAN, set to ws://<this-machine-ip>:4200
#   - For a public deployment with TLS, set to wss://sync.example.com
#
# Must start with ws:// or wss://. Vite only exposes env vars prefixed VITE_.
# VITE_SYNC_URL=ws://192.168.1.42:4200

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sync server (scripts/sync-server.sh) → consumed at npm run sync
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Interface the sync server binds to.
#   - Default (no override): 127.0.0.1 — localhost only, unreachable from other
#     devices. Safe.
#   - 0.0.0.0 — listen on every interface; other devices on the LAN can connect
#     via this machine's IP. Don't do this on an untrusted network.
# SYNC_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Port the sync server listens on. Default 4200. Change only if it clashes.
# SYNC_PORT=4200

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite dev server (not driven by .env — pass via CLI flag)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite binds to localhost by default. To expose the dev server on the LAN:
#     npm run dev -- --host
# That prints both the local and the LAN URL. Combine with SYNC_HOST=0.0.0.0
# + VITE_SYNC_URL=ws://<this-machine-ip>:4200 for cross-device testing.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cross-origin allowlist (shared by Vite dev server AND Better Auth)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated list of origins the SPA + auth-server are reachable
# from beyond their defaults (localhost for Vite, BETTER_AUTH_URL's
# origin for Better Auth). Used when the dev app is accessed via a host
# Vite/BA doesn't know about: Tailscale Serve, ngrok, nip.io, a LAN IP,
# or a custom DNS name.
#
# `scripts/dev-all.sh` sets this automatically when Tailscale Serve is
# detected. Set it manually here only if you want to add OTHER origins
# beyond the auto-detected one.
#
# Vite reads it via vite.config.ts (server.allowedHosts) — bare hostnames
# preferred, but full origins work too (the scheme is stripped).
# Better Auth reads it via scripts/auth-server.sh, which maps it to BA's
# native BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS — BA requires the full origin form,
# so prefer https://host (not bare host) if you want BA-compatible entries.
#
# Examples:
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://nox-work.tail06a0b7.ts.net
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://host-a.ts.net,https://host-b.ts.net
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=*    (allow any — dev convenience only; do NOT set in production)
#
# Legacy overrides (rarely needed; the unified var covers both):
#   VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=…          # Vite only (fallback if ALLOWED_ORIGINS unset)
#   BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=… # BA only (takes precedence over the mapped value)
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://nox-work.tail06a0b7.ts.net

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feedback route → Linear (api server)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal API token for posting Settings → Feedback issues to Linear.
# Get one at: https://linear.app/settings/api → Personal API keys.
# When unset, the api server still boots; the /api/feedback route is
# disabled and the api logs a warning at startup.
# LINEAR_API_TOKEN=lin_api_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tauri shell (Android / desktop) — baked server origin
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical server origin baked into Tauri shell builds (Android/desktop).
# The shell derives sync (wss://<host>/sync/), auth (/api/auth), and
# invite-link origins from this. Web builds ignore it.
# VITE_ARCAN_ORIGIN=https://app.arcan.nox-decima.dev
